  "details": "In VRChat, the “Full Body Tracking Movement Animation” can be set in the settings, but even when this item is turned off, the movement animation is still played.\n\nWe have also observed that the avatar's body moves in an unnatural manner when the movement and jump animations are played back.\n\nWe would like you to correct this problem so that the setting can be switched on and off correctly.\n\nProcedure for occurrence of the bug\n\n1. Launch VRChat in SteamVR mode.\n\n2. Enter full body tracking.\n\n3. Open the menu and go to Settings > Tracking and IK > “Full Body Tracking Movement Animation” and turn it OFF.\n\n4. Use the controller to move and jump.\n\n5. Check that the avatar's body moves in an unnatural way.\n\nRemarks\n\nThe avatars used are Shinra and RadDoll V2.\n\nWe have confirmed that the movement animation settings do not work on the Shinra, Mafuyu and Alfis sample avatars.\n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
